# ENZU build-time configuration (LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` at the repo root and fill in the values, OR export the
# same variables in your shell / CI. The real `.env` is git-ignored and must NOT be
# committed. The runtime APK does NOT read this file — values are baked in at build
# time by build.rs (see docs/enzu/EMBEDDED_SERVER_CONFIG.md).
#
# Precedence: CI environment variables > local .env > built-in ENZU fallback.
# Leave a line unset/absent to use the built-in ENZU default. A value that is
# PRESENT here but invalid (empty, placeholder, localhost, a *.rustdesk.com host,
# or a public key that is not 32 bytes) FAILS the build.
#
# ENZU_PUBLIC_KEY is the RustDesk *server* PUBLIC key (contents of id_ed25519.pub).
# It is public information — never put the private key (id_ed25519) anywhere.

ENZU_ID_SERVER=
ENZU_RELAY_SERVER=
ENZU_PUBLIC_KEY=
